# azd environment state.
#
# .azure/<env>/.env holds the values scripts/env-setup.sh resolves at setup time: the
# subscription id, the SQL admin group's object id, and the resource id of the shared Container
# Apps environment. None of those are secrets — they are public identifiers — but all of them
# are specific to one directory and one subscription, so a committed copy is wrong for anyone
# else who clones this.
#
# It also holds every template OUTPUT azd writes back after a provision, including the SQL
# connection string. That one is safe to print (it ends `Authentication=Active Directory
# Default`, so it names an auth method rather than carrying a credential) but it names live
# infrastructure, and there is no reason for it to be in git.
#
# Recreate it with:  ./scripts/env-setup.sh dev
.azure/
